fact WorkItem(id: "WI-326", description: some(value: "WI-307 v1a follow-on: row subtyping in arrow_compatible. The unify_arrow half of v1a row unification landed (commit 1d62e7a, Rémy/Lindley-Cheney on EffectExpression). The companion arrow_compatible half — open-row subtyping for the covariant-effects check — was NOT shipped and still uses the naive 'each actual ⊆ some(expected)' subset over effects_rows_to_flat_list (typing.rs:6303). PROBLEM: open-tail Var pushed into the flat list fails types_compatible (Var has no functor → false), so any arrow with an open row tail is wrongly rejected against any expected arrow whose tail TermId differs — even when row unification (now available) would absorb the extras. This actively rejects valid subtyping the typer would otherwise accept. SCOPE: replace arrow_compatible's effects-check with a directional row algorithm: actual labels must all be present in expected (or absorbed by expected's open tail); expected's extras may bind actual's open tail. Mirror the unify_effect_rows pattern (typing.rs ~5230) but covariant. Reuse decompose_effect_row + pair_present_labels + bind_row_tail; the only delta is directionality (actual extras MUST be absorbed by expected's tail, not symmetric). Update arrow_compatible signature to take &mut KnowledgeBase (the algorithm allocates fresh tail vars in the both-open case); ripple through types_compatible + is_subtype + entries_cover + ~30 callers + test sites — pure mechanical change like unify_types' signature change in commit 1d62e7a. ACCEPTANCE: open-row subtyping tests (pure ≤ effectful, open ≤ closed with absorbable extras, open ≤ open with shared tail); the closed/closed regression tests (subtype_arrow_fewer_effects, subtype_arrow_different_effects_incompatible) still green; full cargo-test green. Closes the v1a half of WI-307 proposal 045 §Phase 1. Code-review #2 from the WI-307 substrate review (commit 1f92799) resolves under this."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-307"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-28T22:35:04Z"))
